      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T13:00:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This introduces 2 potential future issues. Not concrete bugs now, but we can simply plug both of them right here:\n\nIssue 1: the peerId is mutable. So if the peerId changes between the registration and de-registration, this would remove the wrong key and leave a dead peer in \"peers\" permanently.\n\nIssue 2: there is a potential deadlock issue. The getter is synchronized by peer\u0027s lock and registerPeer() and removeRegistration() call it while holding tracker\u0027s lock. And the reverse order exists as well in BGPPeer - when it registers and closes the registration. There is nothing closing the loop now, but a simple refactor can make that happen.\n\nOne fix for both of these issues: store the peerID into a variable and let the returned registration close using that. With that we\u0027re closing what we registered AND we\u0027re not mixing the locks.",
      "revId": "3f1c32420a6a610b52405b3615d2225feafc3ad4",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
