      "parentUuid": "6b26dd33_9da651c3",
      "revId": "3f1c32420a6a610b52405b3615d2225feafc3ad4",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e42a8d6d_afe4ae50",
        "filename": "bgp/rib-impl/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/protocol/bgp/rib/impl/BGPPeerTrackerImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 8324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T13:00:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This removes whatever is under the peer ID right now, which may be a newer registration for another neighbour that took the same BGP Identifier over — RFC 6286 requires it to be unique only within an AS. Now that the snapshots are rebuilt here, that evicts the live peer and LocRibWriter stops refreshing its adj-rib-out. Could we use peers.remove(peerId, peer) and rebuild only when it removed something?",
      "revId": "3f1c32420a6a610b52405b3615d2225feafc3ad4",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
